msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:5
msgid "`BinFloat`, `BinCoeff`, binary contexts/flags, and binary16/32/64/128 interchange are supported `0.8.0` application APIs. Limb layout, algorithm thresholds, and complete IEEE 754 coverage are not promised."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:9
msgid "This page tracks the `0.8.0` API baseline. The semantic and test scope is in [Conformance](../conformance/bin_float.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:12
#: manual/api/decimal.md:12
#: manual/performance/bin_float.md:10
msgid "Representation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:14
msgid "Finite values are stored as a non-negative `BinCoeff`, an independent sign, and an exponent:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:19
#: manual/api/decimal.md:26
msgid "with an attached working `precision`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:21
msgid "Context, Flags, And Interchange"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:23
msgid "`BinaryRoundingMode`: nearest-even, nearest-away, toward-zero, toward-positive, toward-negative, and away-from-zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:25
msgid "`TininessDetection`: before or after rounding."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:28
msgid "`BinaryFlags`: `inexact`, `underflow`, `overflow`, `division_by_zero`, `invalid_operation`, `combine`, and `to_testfloat_bits`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:30
msgid "`BinaryInterchangeFormat`: binary16, binary32, binary64, binary128 and their precision/exponent metadata."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:32
msgid "`BinaryInterchange::from_hex`, `to_hex`, `to_bin_float`, and `from_bin_float`; `BinFloat::to_interchange`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:35
msgid "`BinaryInterchange::from_bin_float` and `to_interchange` return both encoded bits and status flags."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:38
msgid "Constructors and Observable State"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:53
msgid "`BinCoeff` is the public non-negative coefficient type. Construct one with `BinCoeff::from_uint64`, `BinCoeff::parse`, or `BinCoeff::from_bytes_be`, then pass it to `BinFloat::from_coefficient` or `BinFloat::make`. The sign is the separate `negative?` argument; there is no binary-stack `BigInt` boundary."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/bin_float.md:58
msgid "`BinCoeff` exposes `zero`, `one`, `from_uint64`, `parse`, `from_bytes_be`, `to_uint64`, `to_string`, and `to_bytes_be`; queries include `compare`, `bit_length`, `ctz`, and `test_bit`. Arithmetic includes `add`, `sub_checked`, `mul`, `square`, `div_rem_checked`, `gcd`, `pow_nat`, shifts, and bitwise operations. Subtraction and division are checked because the type cannot represent negative values or division by zero."
msgstr ""

