msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:43
msgid "All scalar cores use the same architectural decomposition even though their representations and standards differ:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:54
msgid "`BinFloat` stores sign, non-negative binary coefficient, exponent, precision, and special state. `Decimal` and GDA `Decimal` independently store sign, package-owned base-`10^9` coefficient, exponent/quantum, precision, and special state. `BallFloat` stores two outward-rounded binary endpoints plus Empty/Entire state; decorated intervals add decoration and NaI without changing the bare representation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:61
msgid "Finalization is the semantic firewall. Coefficient kernels may compute exact products, quotients, roots, or guards, but they do not decide standard flags, cohorts, traps, decorations, or endpoint direction."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:65
msgid "Algorithm Selection Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:67
msgid "Large integer kernels use a staged selector instead of committing to one algorithm:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:79
msgid "Division likewise moves from word and Knuth D to Burnikel-Ziegler and reciprocal Newton where target measurements justify it. Sparse and unbalanced shapes have separate paths because an algorithm selected only by maximum length can waste more work on padding than it saves asymptotically."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:84
msgid "Switch boundaries are private, target-specific policy. They are measured with the Maremark hierarchy across dense, sparse, square, balanced, and unbalanced datasets; boundary tests compare exact results below, at, and above every cutoff. Native, LLVM, Wasm, Wasm-GC, and JavaScript therefore may select different algorithms while returning the same public result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:90
msgid "Certified Elementary Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:92
msgid "Elementary functions share a proof contract across the binary, decimal, and interval stacks:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:95
msgid "produce directed lower and upper enclosures at a working precision;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:96
msgid "round both endpoints to the target domain;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:97
msgid "accept only if target values and observable flags agree;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:98
msgid "otherwise increase precision by `max(32, work / 2)`;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:99
msgid "stop after 12 refinements with structured certification detail."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:101
msgid "`bin_float` owns the scalar dyadic certificates. `ball_float` lifts these certificates over endpoints, critical points, poles, and domains. `decimal` and `decimal_gda` convert exact decimal inputs to directed dyadic bounds and convert certified endpoints back through exact integer arithmetic."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:106
msgid "Total interval APIs may widen to a mathematically safe range such as `[-1,1]` or Entire. `try_*` APIs expose the proof/resource failure instead. Scalar convenience APIs use the same certified path and never substitute a host transcendental approximation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:111
msgid "Context And Effect Flow"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:113
msgid "No numerical package relies on an ambient rounding mode."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:115
msgid "Binary and IEEE decimal contexts are immutable inputs; flags are explicit outputs that callers combine."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:117
msgid "`decimal_gda` returns a new context whose status includes current flags, then chooses a trap in fixed precedence."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:119
msgid "`BallContext` controls outward endpoint precision/exponent bounds and returns interval flags."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:121
msgid "Binary/interval checked wrappers retain the first `ArithmeticError`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:122
msgid "`DecimalChecked` preserves defined IEEE results and accumulates flags while retaining certification errors separately."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:124
msgid "`GdaDecimalChecked` threads one outcome, stops on `Trapped`, and resumes only through an explicit defined-result transition."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:127
msgid "These wrappers compose existing semantics; they do not invent another arithmetic algorithm or merge incompatible effect channels."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:130
msgid "Parsing And Execution"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:132
msgid "`numeric_expr` contains syntax data and post-order callback evaluation. It performs no IO and selects no numeric backend."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:135
msgid "Each `frontend/*` package owns one external grammar:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:137
msgid "`gda_expr` parses `.decTest` directives/cases and executes GDA outcomes;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:138
msgid "`testfloat_expr` parses TestFloat vectors and binds format, rounding, tininess;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:139
msgid "`mpfr_expr` parses pinned MPFR square-root, power, and elementary witnesses;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:140
msgid "`itl_expr` parses interval test rows and classifies the declared support set."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:142
msgid "Frontends return typed summaries. CLI packages own files, filters, shards, rendering, and exit codes. Python tools fetch checksum-pinned data, plan tasks, run isolated targets/processes, and aggregate results; they do not replace the MoonBit numerical implementation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:147
msgid "Stable And Internal Boundaries"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:149
msgid "The application-facing release surfaces are `def`, the concrete numeric packages, and checked wrappers. `semantic` and `numeric_expr` are provisional integration surfaces. Frontends are public so repository runners can compose them, but compatibility is limited to declared corpora and generated interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture.md:154
msgid "`internal/*`, CLI packages, `bench/*`, `consistency`, and `doc_examples` are implementation/verification infrastructure. A symbol may appear in `pkg.generated.mbti` without becoming a long-term application contract; read the package design page before depending on it."
msgstr ""

