#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:3
#: manual/performance_audit.md:121
msgid "Claim"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:5
msgid "The current strict ITF1788 gate executes 4,656/4,656 selected cases with no failed, unsupported, or diagnostic rows. This is a claim about the pinned corpus revision, selected operation phases, and runner precision—not a claim of complete IEEE 1788 implementation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:7
msgid "Semantic Oracle"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:9
msgid "Expected results are compared by set meaning: endpoint containment, set relations, boolean relations, overlap states, numeric observations, and decorations use operation-specific comparators. A conservative interval may be valid when the contract permits widening; an enclosure that excludes an exact result is never valid."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:11
msgid "Supported Phases"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:13
msgid "The strict matrix covers sets, relations, observations, cancellation, add/subtract/multiply/divide, elementary core, exponential/logarithmic functions, general power, trigonometric functions including `atan2`, FMA, integer power, and extrema. Phase operation sets are disjoint so a row is never counted twice."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:15
msgid "Decorations And Fallbacks"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:17
msgid "Empty, Entire, and decorated NaI are separate states. Elementary kernels use directed dyadic certificates. When range reduction cannot be certified, `sin`/`cos` return `[-1,1]` and `tan` returns Entire; that preserves inclusion but does not promise tightness."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:19
msgid "Exclusions"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/ball_float.md:21
msgid "Reverse interval operations, every decoration rule outside the selected phases, arbitrary endpoint formats, and unpinned upstream revisions remain outside the claim."
msgstr ""

