#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:20
msgid "Embed An Exact Dyadic Point"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:22
msgid "`exact` means exact with respect to the supplied `BinFloat` value."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:38
msgid "If a smaller interval precision is requested, construction rounds the lower endpoint downward and upper endpoint upward. It never silently drops the source dyadic point."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:42
msgid "Build A Valid Range"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:44
msgid "Use `from_bounds` when endpoints are already known. Use `try_from_bounds` when input order or finiteness is not trusted."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:60
msgid "`new(center, radius)` is useful for measurements, but remember that storage and all set operations use lower/upper endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:63
msgid "Enclose A Decimal Real Value Correctly"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:65
msgid "A nearest-rounded decimal-to-binary conversion followed by `exact` encloses only the resulting binary point. To enclose the original decimal, convert in both directions and use both bounds."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:87
msgid "Use this pattern at decimal/binary boundaries, then keep calculations in the interval domain."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:90
msgid "Read Set Relations"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:109
msgid "Use `contains` for point inclusion, `subset`/`interior` for set containment, `overlap_state` for geometry, and `definitely_lt`/`definitely_gt` only when an order statement must hold for every point. Do not sort intervals with a scalar comparison rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:114
msgid "Perform Outward-Rounded Arithmetic"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:116
msgid "Ordinary interval arithmetic preserves enclosure:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:124
msgid "Division by an interval that crosses zero returns Entire because every real value may be approached. A denominator with a one-sided zero endpoint may yield a half-infinite enclosure. These are valid set results, not generic failures."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:128
msgid "Use `BallContext` when endpoint precision/exponent limits and flags matter:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:136
msgid "Choose Total Or Checked Elementary Operations"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:138
msgid "Total operations always return a valid enclosure. If certification cannot establish a tight trigonometric range, `sin_interval`/`cos_interval` may return `[-1, 1]`, and `tan_interval` may return Entire."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:159
msgid "Choose the family according to application policy:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:161
msgid "use `try_*_interval` when resource/range proof failure must stop or be logged;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:162
msgid "use total `*_interval` when continued calculation with a conservative enclosure is preferred;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:164
msgid "test `is_entire()` or width when tightness is an acceptance criterion."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:166
msgid "Use Decorations When Domain Quality Matters"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:181
msgid "Decorations can weaken after domain clipping or discontinuity. NaI is distinct from Empty: NaI records an invalid decorated operation, while Empty is a valid set with no members."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:185
#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:44
#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:180
#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:52
#: manual/tutorial/decimal.md:191
#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:78
#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda.md:175
#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:80
msgid "Recommended Practice"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:187
msgid "Construct intervals from outward-rounded bounds at every representation boundary."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:189
msgid "Keep all intermediate calculations in `BallFloat`; extracting a midpoint loses enclosure information."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:191
msgid "Use set relations rather than scalar equality/order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:192
msgid "Decide explicitly whether proof failure should produce an error (`try_*`) or a conservative range (total API)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:194
msgid "Check width/Entire separately from correctness: an enclosure can be correct but too wide for the application."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:196
msgid "Use decorated intervals only when decoration/NaI semantics are actually part of the contract; otherwise bare intervals are simpler."
msgstr ""

