#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:1
msgid "`ball_float_checked` Tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:3
msgid "`BallFloatResult` keeps `Result[BallFloat, ArithmeticError]` inside a fluent pipeline. Use it when invalid bounds, non-finite exact construction, or a checked elementary proof failure should stop later interval operations."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:7
msgid "Validate Construction Once"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:23
msgid "Later operations short-circuit the first error. Use `map` for an infallible interval transform and `bind` when a callback may construct another checked interval. `flat_map` is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:27
msgid "Distinguish Wide Success From Failure"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:29
msgid "Entire is a valid success because it still encloses the mathematical result. For example, division by an interval crossing zero may produce Entire rather than `ArithmeticError`. After extracting a successful interval, apply an application tightness policy with `is_entire()`, `width()`, or boundedness."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:34
msgid "Relation observers such as `contains`, `subset`, and `overlaps` remain outside the wrapper. Extract the checked interval, then apply the observer; a Boolean relation has no meaningful first-error pipeline state."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:38
msgid "Decorations And Flags Stay Explicit"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:40
msgid "`BallFloatResult` stores bare intervals only. It does not retain `BallFloatDecorated` state or `BallFlags`. Use raw `ball_float` APIs when decoration, NaI, inexact, overflow, or underflow is part of the result contract."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:46
msgid "Use the wrapper to validate untrusted construction and retain first failure."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:47
msgid "Treat Entire as successful enclosure, then evaluate tightness separately."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:48
msgid "Extract once before set relations or decorated operations."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:49
msgid "Use raw `try_*_interval` when structured certification detail must be handled directly."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:52
msgid "See [Design](../design/ball_float_checked.md) and the raw [`ball_float` tutorial](ball_float.md)."
msgstr ""

