msgid "Published Claims"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:42
msgid "**GDA:** all 64,986 legal executable scalar rows in the 144-file `official` corpus pass; all 16,124 legal rows in `official0` pass. The 141 `#` placeholder/non-scalar invalid rows are diagnostic exclusions, not unsupported legal behavior."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:46
msgid "**Binary:** 7,461,360 TestFloat vectors cover binary16/32/64/128 add, subtract, multiply, divide, and square root, five rounding directions, and both tininess modes. The pinned MPFR square-root dataset adds 1,055 rows."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:49
msgid "**IEEE decimal:** committed decimal32/64/128 DPD and BID fixtures cover encoding, special values, flags, core arithmetic, and all 1,024 DPD declets on native, Wasm, Wasm-GC, and JavaScript. LLVM is excluded from this gate."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:52
msgid "**Interval:** the strict ITF1788 phases cover declared set, relation, observation, arithmetic, cancellation, elementary, power, trigonometric, FMA, integer-power, and extrema operations. Reverse operations remain unsupported."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:57
msgid "These are finite claims. They do not imply every IEEE 754 or IEEE 1788 operation, arbitrary resource sizes, every NaN payload policy, or unpinned future corpus revisions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:61
msgid "Reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:63
msgid "External artifacts are revision- and SHA-256-pinned in corpus manifests. Builds use backend-named outputs and isolated target directories so parallel jobs do not overwrite one another. Shards select deterministic case indices, and merged summaries retain exact totals and failed IDs."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:68
msgid "The MoonBit frontend parses and executes numeric rows. Python orchestrates downloads, task planning, subprocesses, target selection, and aggregation. An optional oracle is never silently replaced by a weaker implementation; missing requirements must be reported explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:73
msgid "Performance evidence is separate from semantic conformance. Benchmark manifests pin baseline source, dependencies, toolchain, target, schedule, sample count, and dispersion limits. A performance threshold never changes correctness."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:77
msgid "Failure Triage"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:79
msgid "Re-run the failing backend with the smallest case, ID filter, phase, or shard that reproduces it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:81
msgid "Distinguish parse diagnostics, unsupported cases, legacy classifications, executable mismatches, and infrastructure failures."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:83
msgid "Record expected value, actual value, flags, context, target, corpus revision, and command."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:85
msgid "Run the matching white-box package test to decide whether the defect is in parsing, arithmetic, interchange, or aggregation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:87
msgid "After a fix, run the focused case, committed smoke fixture, backend gate, and finally `just pr` or `just ci` as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:90
msgid "Do not weaken strict support, discard flags, or change the denominator to make a failing gate pass."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:93
msgid "Release Gate"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:95
msgid "Before publishing:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:97
msgid "align `moon.mod`, root README, localized indexes, standards, and changelog;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:98
msgid "run `just docs` and inspect generated interface differences;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:99
msgid "run `just pr` during iteration;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:100
msgid "run `just ci` for the release candidate;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:101
msgid "publish through the repository GitHub Actions workflow."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:103
msgid "Local `moon publish` is not the Luna-Flow release path because organization credentials are supplied by the workflow."
msgstr ""
